{
  "name": "relation-confirmed-contradicted-and-unconfirmable",
  "acceptance_item": 6,
  "note": "The distinction the product did not have when it replicated for months over data with no off-site copy: an edge observed at both ends is not the same statement as an edge observed at one. /srv is asserted from both vantages with the same facts and is confirmed; /var is asserted from both and they disagree, which is contradicted \u2014 a STATE, not a merge conflict and not a silent win for either vantage; and the devices side declares it cannot be confirmed from the far end, so it stays honestly asserted even though a mount did assert back at it. A type is judged by its own declaration, never by whether some other assertion happens to point the right way.",
